Because x265 is GPL-2.0-or-later, and GPL has no static-linking exception, distributing a
static library that embeds x265 makes the resulting archive a combined GPL work: anyone who
redistributes it (including the release tarballs from this repo) must also satisfy the GPL,
such as making the corresponding source available and keeping the GPL notice attached.
libheif and libde265 are LGPL-3.0, which does permit static linking, but still requires
satisfying LGPLv3 section 4 (e.g. providing the object files needed to relink against a
modified version of the library).

To produce an artifact without the GPL obligation, build with WITH_X265=OFF in build.sh; the
remaining libraries (libheif, libde265: LGPL-3.0; libaom, dav1d, libwebp: BSD) still apply
their own terms, but none of them are GPL.
